Logical Operators = &&, ||, !, used to combine or modify boolean expressions
&& = and, where condition must be true
|| = or, where at least one condition must be true
! = not, where the condition is inverted, reverse the true or false value

Examples: 
 bool isSunny = true;


    if (!isSunny) {
        printf("It is cloudy");
    }
    else {
        printf("It is sunny");
    }

 if (temp > 0 || temp < 30) {
        printf("The temperature is GOOD");
    }
    else {
        printf("The temperature is BAD");
    }

if (temp > 0 && temp < 30) {
        printf("The temperature is GOOD");
    }
    else {
        printf("The temperature is BAD");
    }
